{
    "_comment": "UKI disk layout — UEFI-only, no BIOS boot. See http://www.chromium.org/chromium-os/building-chromium-os/disk-layout-format",
    "metadata": {
        "_comment": "Partitions are aligned to 2MB (4096 blocks). For the sake of VHD disks sizes should align to *both* 2MB and a CHS cylender boundry for the common 16H 63S geometry (16*63 = 1008 blocks). The least common multiple of 4096 and 1008 is 258048 blocks.",
        "part_alignment": 4096,
        "disk_alignment": 258048,
        "block_size": 512,
        "fs_block_size": 4096
    },
    "layouts": {
        "base": {
            "1": {
                "_comment": "128 MiB -> 192 MiB (blocks are 512-byte sectors). UKI boot keeps kernel+initramfs on the ESP, and the acl-t UKI rebuilt by Image Customizer needs more headroom than stock.",
